<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Rate on Yugoslav central bank bonds unchanged.</title>
<headline>Rate on Yugoslav central bank bonds unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Yugoslavia (NBY) left the interest rate on its short-term bonds auctioned on Tuesday unchanged at a monthly three percent, the Belgrade bourse said.</p>
<p>The three percent monthly rate corresponds to an annual 41.63 percent.</p>
<p>The NBY offered for sale a new 60-million dinars tranche of 20-day bonds, issued at a 10,000 dinars face value, and sold 19 million dinars worth, the bourse said.</p>
<p>-- Gordana Kukic, Belgrade Newsroom +381 11 311 4254</p>
</text>
